# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored; .env.local.example is committed as a template.
#
# Where to find these:
#   1. Open https://supabase.com/dashboard
#   2. Pick your project (or create one)
#   3. Project Settings → API
#   4. Copy "Project URL" and the "anon public" key (NOT the service_role key)
#
# If you'd rather run Supabase locally:
#   brew install supabase/tap/supabase
#   supabase start
# The CLI prints the local URL and anon key when it boots.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional — lets users connect their own GA4 account from the app.
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Web application in Google Cloud and add:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/google-analytics/oauth/callback
#   https://your-domain.com/api/google-analytics/oauth/callback
# as authorized redirect URIs.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional legacy/server fallback — only needed if you prefer service-account GA4 access.
# Provide either GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON (one-line JSON blob) OR
# the email + private key pair.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional — Plausible UTM reporting. The destination website must have
# Plausible installed. This app uses the Stats API key server-side and stores
# each project's Plausible site ID/domain in Supabase.
# PLAUSIBLE_API_KEY=
# PLAUSIBLE_API_BASE_URL=https://plausible.io
#
# Optional — track usage of this internal Next app itself with Plausible.
# Use the site-specific script URL from Plausible, e.g.
# https://plausible.io/js/pa-XXXXX.js. Leave blank to disable.
# PLAUSIBLE_SCRIPT_SRC=
# PLAUSIBLE_API_ENDPOINT=
# PLAUSIBLE_CAPTURE_LOCALHOST=false

# Optional — Postiz social publishing bridge. Postiz owns OAuth, social account
# connections, provider rules, retries, and final publishing. This app only
# submits approved creatives to the Postiz Public API and stores local receipts.
# Use https://api.postiz.com for Postiz Cloud, or your self-hosted instance base.
# POSTIZ_API_KEY=
# POSTIZ_API_BASE_URL=https://api.postiz.com

# Optional — Sentry error tracking. Leave blank for local dev. To activate:
#   1. Create a project at https://sentry.io
#   2. Copy the DSN into both vars below (server + client).
#   3. (Optional) For source map upload during deploy, add an auth token:
#      https://sentry.io/settings/account/api/auth-tokens/  with `project:releases`
# Errors only fire when NODE_ENV=production, so dev stays quiet either way.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
